   "attributes": {
    "id": 587477,
    "title": "Best Poster Competition Report",
    "description": "<h1>Best Poster Competition Report</h1>\r\n<p><strong>Organizing Entities:</strong> IEEE Women in Engineering &ndash; Jordan Section (IEEE WIE JS), in collaboration with IEEE Women in Engineering &ndash; Mutah University (IEEE WIE MU).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Hosting Entity:</strong> Entrepreneurship and Innovation Center &ndash; Mutah University.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Event Date:</strong> Thursday, October 29, 2026.</p>\r\n<h2>Overview</h2>\r\n<p>IEEE Women in Engineering &ndash; Jordan Section (IEEE WIE JS), in collaboration with IEEE Women in Engineering &ndash; Mutah University (IEEE WIE MU), plans to organize the <strong>Best Poster Competition</strong>, a student competition targeting undergraduate students in Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM) disciplines from universities across Jordan.</p>\r\n<p>The competition aims to encourage students to present their scientific projects and technical ideas in an innovative and professional manner. It also seeks to develop their skills in scientific poster design, communication, and public presentation, while providing opportunities to discuss their projects and receive feedback from academics and professionals.</p>\r\n<h2>Target Audience and Participation</h2>\r\n<p>The competition is open to undergraduate students enrolled in STEM-related disciplines at Jordanian universities. Participation may be individual or in teams of one to three students, with at least one team member required to hold active membership in IEEE Women in Engineering (IEEE WIE).</p>\r\n<p>Approximately 60 students are expected to participate, with total attendance estimated at around 100 people, including participants, judges, faculty members, organizers, and guests.</p>\r\n<h2>Competition Format</h2>\r\n<p>The competition will include an official announcement and registration period, an online introductory session, and two online training workshops covering scientific poster design and presentation skills. Participants will then be given time to prepare and refine their posters, followed by a preliminary evaluation to select the finalists.</p>\r\n<p>The final round is planned to take place in person at Mutah University, in coordination with the Entrepreneurship and Innovation Center. Participants will present their posters to a specialized judging panel, followed by the announcement of results and recognition of the winners.</p>\r\n<h2>Event Date and Venue</h2>\r\n<p>The final round is scheduled for <strong>Thursday, October 29, 2026</strong>, at Mutah University, in coordination with the Entrepreneurship and Innovation Center. Final arrangements regarding the venue and required facilities will be completed in coordination with the relevant parties.</p>\r\n<p>The proposed logistical requirements include providing a suitable space for displaying posters, poster stands for presenting projects, and refreshments and lunch for participants and attendees, subject to available resources and the agreement between the organizing and hosting entities.</p>\r\n<h2>Expected Impact</h2>\r\n<p>The competition is expected to enhance students&rsquo; scientific and technical communication skills, encourage innovation and creativity, and provide a platform for knowledge sharing and experience exchange among students from Jordanian universities. It will also strengthen collaboration between IEEE WIE communities and the Entrepreneurship and Innovation Center in supporting student initiatives.</p>\r\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Best Poster Competition</strong> is a student-focused initiative designed to support creativity and showcase scientific, engineering, and technical projects in an academic and competitive environment. The competition aims to promote a culture of innovation and scientific communication among university students across Jordan.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Organizing Entities:</strong> IEEE Women in Engineering &ndash; Jordan Section (IEEE WIE JS), in collaboration with IEEE Women in Engineering &ndash; Mutah University (IEEE WIE MU).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Hosting Entity:</strong> Entrepreneurship and Innovation Center &ndash; Mutah University.</p>",
